      "message": "New incoming external reports: sub-exponential 3SAT / ETH packets\n\nCommit, unchanged and as delivered, the five sub-exponential 3SAT (ETH)\narrivals that the drop process had staged but not committed, so that each\nstays recoverable after the placement commit retires it (docs/incoming\nREADME, section 1):\n\n- cauchy_mode_improvement_2026-10-26.zip (603,205 bytes): factorial\n  Cauchy modes for the contraction of the OpenAI ETH preprint.\n- eth_contraction_improvements.zip (462,089 bytes): tapered Hermite\n  count, revised contraction schedule, streamed packet extraction.\n- sat_density_improvement.zip (476,245 bytes): clause-density-aware\n  exact k-SAT counting.\n- paper.pdf (887,884 bytes): OpenAI, \"The Exponential Time Hypothesis is\n  False\" (25 October 2026), byte-identical to paper.pdf in\n  openai/math@7ef5c0cc5ca4b0e072b7a050fca09ab24bc6fa3a.\n- eth.pdf (868,673 bytes): \"A 2^{o(n)} time algorithm for 3-SAT\"\n  (26 October 2026), a separate 49-page manuscript.\n\nPath-limited: no other staged or modified path is included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "files": [
        "docs/incoming/cauchy_mode_improvement_2026-10-26.zip",
        "docs/incoming/eth.pdf",
